#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
verify_rp2_skipped.py (v2) — provenance-gated verification harness for the RP2
previously-skipped tests (54 knowledge + 1 compatibility) of the Memory-Integrity /
Claude-Mon project.

v2 implements the remediation of every defect found in the 2026-11-02 audit of v1:
  D1  source identity is satisfied by Git route (clean tree at exact commit) OR archive
      route (byte-exact, safely-extracted user archive + authoritative manifest);
      a valid archive no longer blocks. Git-route failure alone is NOT a missing input.
  D2  test imports: runner cwd/PYTHONPATH point at memory-integrity/tests_v2 (nested
      layout); an import-origin probe records the ACTUAL loaded module file for every
      executed module; import errors and unittest _FailedTest placeholders are refused.
  D3  compatibility group: the 4 original test sources + wrapper snapshot are restored
      from the delivered Archive-Manifest.json mapping, byte-verified (wrapper pinned
      externally), the UNMODIFIED wrapper is imported and the accepted test id is
      selected from the wrapper's own suite; the selected test's class module file must
      resolve to a restored original.
  D4  reconciliation: execution records are an append-only LIST (no dict overwrite);
      rejects duplicate executions, unexpected ids, missing ids, incomplete captures and
      any non-PASS outcome; executed set must EQUAL the 55-id expectation set exactly.
  D5  archive checks: path containment via path COMPONENTS (not string prefix); symlink
      / non-regular / absolute / '..' members rejected; extracted file set must equal
      manifest set exactly; dirty git tree rejects Git route.
  D6  exit codes: 0 only for RP2_PREVIOUSLY_SKIPPED_LINUX_TESTS_VERIFIED; 1 verification
      failed; 2 provenance blocked; 3 setup/harness error.
  D7  report: the "why" narrative is derived from the ACTUAL failed gate items /
      reconciliation anomalies — no hardcoded missing-source story.
  D8  self-tests: --selftest runs boundary checks over clearly-labelled SYNTHETIC
      fixtures (valid archive through full gate, nested tests_v2 import probe, duplicate
      records, wrapper restore/load path, traversal rejection, dirty-tree rejection,
      skip classification, exit-code map). No model downloads, no RP2 bytes claimed.

The harness NEVER reports PASS for an unexecuted, mocked or blocked test:
unexecuted => NOT_EXECUTED, environment-forbidden => BLOCKED.

Verdicts: RP2_PREVIOUSLY_SKIPPED_LINUX_TESTS_VERIFIED | VERIFICATION_FAILED |
BLOCKED_MISSING_REQUIRED_INPUTS | SETUP_BLOCKED | HARNESS_ERROR | NOT_SET.
"""

